{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "PvP class and specialization tuning (#250)",
  "contract": [
    "Spell.dbc holds a PvP twin 100 ids above each normal tuning aura (887100-887190, same name, class and specialization as 887000-887090). Every twin is a passive self aura with effect 0 aura 322, effect 1 aura 87 with MiscValueB 1 and effect 2 aura 136 or a dummy.",
    "Aura 322 is damage done against players: Fire and Ice 1582385 reads '$s1% ($s2% against players)' with aura 341 on $s1 and aura 322 on $s2, and Zandalari Windreaver Global pvp mod 301115 (aura 322 -10) reads 'Reduces damage versus player by 10%'. Aura 87 MiscValueB 1 is damage taken from players and 2 from creatures: Libram of Tenacity 801461 reads 'Physical Damage taken by $s2% ($s3% against players)' with MiscValueB 2 on $s2 and 1 on $s3.",
    "Native SpellEffectInfo::CalcValue at level 60: Chronomancer Class 887110 effect 0 EffectBasePoints -11 + DieSides 1 = -10; Templar Class 887107 effect 0 -11 + floor(50 x -0.4) + 1 = -30; Reaper Domination 887183 effect 0 -3 + floor(50 x -0.56) + 1 = -30 and effect 1 9 + floor(50 x 0.5) + 1 = 35.",
    "Chronomancer Time 887054/887154 and the normal Chronomancer Class 887010 hold zero damage adjustments, so a Time Chronomancer deals 90% against a player of what it deals against a creature.",
    "The twins' aura 136 carries no target or PvP scope (Bloodmage Class 887108 -8, Primalist Class 887119 -8, Sun Cleric Blessings 887172 +10), so whether it belongs to PvP only is unresolved; the healing effect is held inert and this scenario guards that the PvP twin leaves healing unchanged."
  ],
